==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|leyfa}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*laubijaną|*(uz)laubijaną}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈleiːva/}}
* {{rhymes|is|eiːva}}
* {{homophones|is|leifa}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-weak|leyfði|leyft}}

# {{lb|is|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[allow]] something, to [[permit]] something, to [[give]] [[permission]] for something
# {{lb|is|ditransitive|governs the accusative and dative}} to [[allow]] somebody something, to [[permit]] somebody something, to [[give]] somebody [[permission]] for something
#* Timothy 2:11-12 ([http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=1+Timothy+2:11-12&version=NIV English], [http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=1%20Timothy%202:11-12&version=ICELAND Icelandic])
#*: ''Konan á að læra í kyrrþey, í allri undirgefni. Ekki '''leyfi''' ég konu að kenna eða taka sér vald yfir manninum, heldur á hún að vera kyrrlát.''
#*:: A woman should learn in quietness and full submission. I do not '''permit''' a woman to teach or to have authority over a man; she must be silent.
#: ''Ég '''leyfði''' honum að [[leika sér]] með boltann.''
#:: I '''gave''' him '''permission''' to play with his ball.

